A||N||13||bHooper||Can u replace exhaust manifolds...||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||12-28-2000||09:36 AM||||while the engine is in the car?  My '86GT has a bethy (sp) of exhaust leaks, and I expect that they start at the manifold.  Is it possible to change them with the engine in the car?<P>How much time should I alow for?  I wouild guess that I need to remove the A/C compressor and other things to get to the front one, any other surprises?<P><BR>Thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||12-28-2000||11:25 AM||||hoop, you can change them in the car - we do it here all the time - take the deck lid off, it's much easier that way. Also, for the front manifold you can remove the rear cradle bolts and tilt the engine down - it makes it much easier to get to the front manifold - yes, move that A/C thing out of the way!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||12-28-2000||12:13 PM||||tgowens is right, that's the best way. My 86SE had the same problem. My mechanic and I decided the best thing to do in my case, not the easiest, was to remove the engine. With the engine out, he easily drilled out the missing studs, replaced the gaskets, and manifolds. While it was out, we went ahead and put new plugs in, water pump, cleaned lots of brackets, wrapped the turbo outlet, cleaned and painted the engine bay area...... ||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||12-28-2000||12:50 PM||||Terry,  is the alignment affected, when you drop the front part of the cradle?  do I have to disconect the struts?<P>what problems should I expect to encounter?<P>thanks!<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||12-28-2000||01:03 PM||||The below link is an article I wrote for our club on installing Sprint Manifolds. It has details on removing the exhaust manifolds with the engine in the car. (and installing the sprints') The A/C does not need to be removed on some cars (depends on the compressor GM used. I think there are a few different ones.) Also some cars require the coolant tube that runs along the back side of the engine to be loosened in order to access the bottom and top bolt on the far right side of the manifold. My 86 did not but I helped a member of the club with his 87 GT and we had to do it on his car.<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-sprintheaders.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-sprintheaders.html</A> <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||dman||12-28-2000||05:02 PM||||Hello everyone. <P>Bhooper, to tilt the cradle you will remove the -REAR- cradle bolts, not the front ones. Your dogbone will ensure it doesn't drop too far down. When you do this the rear drops down a few inches exposing more of the front. You don't need to disconnect anything to tilt the cradle, you're just tilting it...not dropping it. There is plenty of slack on all the lines and cables to allow you to do this. Since everything is left intact you don't have to worry about realignment or anything like that.<p>[This message has been edited by dman (edited 12-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||12-28-2000||05:42 PM||||thats good to know.  i have plenty of experience dropping the cradle, i know that there is enough slack to do most things.<P>what aobut removeing manifold bolts... anything in particular to do, or worry about?<BR>(i am probably not going to do this for a bit, but i am getting tired of the exhaust leaks)<P>thanks!<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mark||12-28-2000||05:57 PM||||To gain better access to the front manifold, I removed the exhaust system from the joint at the "Y" pipe on back.  Easy enough to get off, but the springs are a bit of a pain to get back on.  And yes, you do have to remove (but not disconnect) the A/C compressor to get at one manifold bolt.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||12-29-2000||04:25 PM||||make sure u WD40 the bolts the nite before. Hopefully none of the studs will break. on my 2 manifolds 5 of them broke, had to drill and retap them-and make sure that you use either grade 8 bolts, or studs with nuts, preferably stainless so they wont break next time.<P>oh yea i took cyndis pic off my hood, lol<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||bHooper||12-29-2000||05:09 PM||||when i do this (probably summertime), where do i get the studs?  are they all standard size?<P>if it's better to use them, versus bolts, i want to do the right thing, when i go about it.<P>thanks!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||12-29-2000||06:27 PM||||I think I have a couple of new exhaust studs laying around here that you can have. I didn't use them on mine since they are only used to hold the heat sheild and with sprint manifolds you can't use them. I'll look tomorrow and if I can find them I'll let you know via Email.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||bHooper||12-29-2000||07:58 PM||||thanks!  but remember, this isnt a project that i'm gonna do anytime soon.  i just want to know everything that there is to know, b4 i tackle it.<P>heck, after the 2 month suspension job... the little lady ain't gonna let me spend more than a few hours here and there working on it, for a bit.<P>i'll probably do this in the summer, maybe late spring.<P>but if you can spare one, i can definatly match it up somewhere!<P>Thanks!<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000012||bHooper||02-17-2001||04:12 PM||||well, i started working on the front manifold, this weekend.  <P>so far i have removed the decklid, rear cradle bolts, and heat shield.  i'm currentl letting the bolts/studs soak in pb blaster.<P>anyone have any tips for removeing the studs?  do they come out with the flange nut, or do i have to buy some special tool?<P>i'm hoping to do this tomorrow.<P>thanks!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000013||bHooper||02-17-2001||10:39 PM||||well, i got the manifold out.  would you believe that the bolt, below the manifold to crossover flange was loose!  not only that, but once removed i discovered that the gasket was only protecting 2 banks!<P>tomorrow, the fun begins... reinstallation.<P>also, look for my new thread, titled "so i have this dipstick tube, where does it go?"<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
